        "original_id": "e3854274-a654-50b0-802c-edab248c59be",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Castor McCord, Louis Armstrong\n- Places: Ohio, Atlantic City, New York City\n- Organizations: Mills Blue Rhythm Band\n- Topics: jazz\n\nFacts:\n- Later in the 1920s, Castor McCord moved from Ohio to Atlantic City and then to New York City.\n- In the late 1920s, Castor McCord played with the Mills Blue Rhythm Band and with Louis Armstrong in New York City.\n- Louis Armstrong was born on August 4, 1901, and died on July 6, 1971.\n- Louis Armstrong was nicknamed Satchmo, Satch, and Pops.\n- Louis Armstrong was an American trumpeter, composer, singer, and occasional actor.\n- Louis Armstrong was one of the most influential figures in jazz.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
